```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;

public class Main {
    public static String wordWrap(String filePath, int width) {
        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(filePath))) {
            StringBuilder wrappedText = new StringBuilder();
            long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                if (line.length() <= width) {
                    wrappedText.append(line).append("\n");
                } else {
                    String[] words = line.split("\\s+");
                    for (int i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
                        if (i > 0) {
                            wrappedText.insert(i * width + 1, " ");
                        }
                        wrappedText.append(words[i]);
                        if (i < words.length - 1) {
                            wrappedText.insert(i * width + 2, " ");
                        }
                    }
                }

                long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
                if ((endTime - startTime) > 10)
                    return null;
            }

            return wrappedText.toString().trim();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            // handle exception
            return null;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String filePath = "path_to_your_file";
        int width = 20;

        System.out.println(wordWrap(filePath, width));
    }
}
```

This code uses a `BufferedReader` to read the file line by line and then splits each line into words. It inserts spaces between words according to the specified width.

Please note that you should replace `"path_to_your_file"` with the actual path to your text file.

Also, this code assumes that the input file is in the same directory as the Java program. If it's not, you need to provide the full path to the file.

You can modify this code further based on your specific requirements.
